            <ArticleTitle>[Unstable angina with subvalvular aortic stenosis in a 65-year-old woman].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of 65-year-old woman with unstable angina, who was admitted to our institution. Physical examination revealed the presence of a systolic cardiac murmur. Transthoracic echocardiography showed subvalvular aortic stenosis. The patient underwent successful coronary artery by-pass surgery and myectomy surgery. Diagnosis and treatment of subvalvular stenosis coexistent with coronary artery disease are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
